# Progressive Disclosure Tooling

Agents must discover available help before executing work, without loading unnecessary context.

## Required Discovery Step

After reading `.cursor/rules/` and before substantive planning or coding:

1. Read `.cursor/skills/SKILLS_CATALOG.md`.
2. Select the skills whose category, name, or description fits the user request.
3. Read only the selected skill `SKILL.md` files and any directly referenced files required for the task.
4. If the task can use an MCP server, inspect the relevant MCP descriptor folder first:
   - `/Users/linktrend/.cursor/projects/Users-linktrend-Projects-LiNKtrend-System/mcps`
   - `.cursor/mcp.json`
5. If a Cursor plugin appears relevant, inspect plugin-provided skills/rules/assets under `/Users/linktrend/.cursor/plugins/cache` before relying on memory.

## Selection Rules

- Prefer LiNKtrend project rules and project skills over imported generic skills when they conflict.
- Use imported GStack skills as optional workflow accelerators; they do not override `.cursor/rules/` or direct user instructions.
- Do not read every skill body at startup. The catalog is the routing layer.
- Always inspect an MCP tool schema/descriptor before calling that MCP tool.
- Follow all always-applied Cursor rules even when a selected skill suggests a different workflow.
